# Accepted risks for the Trivy IaC scan (reviewed 2026-11-13).
# Each entry needs a reason; revisit if the threat model or data changes.

# AWS-0011: CloudFront without WAF.
# The distribution serves two small, public, read-only JSON files (GET/HEAD only,
# cached at the edge). A WAF web ACL costs >= ~$5-8/month, which outweighs the risk
# for this project. Mitigations: private bucket via OAC, TLS 1.2+, AWS Shield Standard,
# budget alarm. Add WAF with a rate-based rule if the feed ever serves private data.
AVD-AWS-0011

# AWS-0132: S3 encrypted with SSE-S3 (AES-256) instead of a customer-managed KMS key.
# The bucket only holds a feed derived from ICEYE's public CC BY 4.0 open data, so
# key-level access control adds no protection; a CMK costs $1/month plus requests.
AVD-AWS-0132
